# What this repo is

Personal ESPHome project. Contents:

- `components/` — custom external ESPHome components. Source of truth, consumed by configs via `external_components: github://idlezombie/esphome@<branch-or-tag>`.
- `devices/` — reference / backup copies of device YAML configs.

# What this repo is NOT

- It is **not** a self-contained ESPHome project.
- `common.yaml` and `secrets.yaml` live inside the ESPHome Builder install, not in this repo.
- Do **not** run `esphome config` / `esphome compile` against `devices/*.yaml`. They `!include common.yaml`, which is intentionally absent here.
- The actual deployed configs are edited and built inside ESPHome Builder; the device YAMLs here are reference copies.

# Dev workflow

- One branch per component or device under development (e.g. `actron_modbus`, `mpu6050_tilt`, `feeder`). Even single-file device-only work gets its own branch.
- `main` holds things that have been flashed and verified.
- Prefer pinning device configs to tags/commits once a component is stable; use branches during active development.

# Tooling

- Repo is open in both Cursor and Sublime Merge. Only one tool should perform git mutations (commit / checkout / rebase) at a time. Read-only operations in parallel are fine.
- This machine: Windows + PowerShell. `git` is not on `PATH`; use the Git bundled with Sublime Merge: `C:\Program Files\Sublime Merge\Git\cmd\git.exe`.
- Never commit `secrets.yaml` or anything matching `.gitignore`.
